{"results":[{"record_id":"full_2026-07-06__rec_003627","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"SEAL is presented as a new vision-omics self-supervised framework over paired spatial transcriptomics and histology, with a VAE/encoder-decoder for image-to-gene reconstruction. The record shows no natural-language text or text-bio alignment, so it is excluded for lacking a text component.","evidence_snippet":"\"paired H&E morphology image patches and corresponding Visium ST spots\"; \"align the transcriptomics and histomorphology embeddings\"; \"train a transcriptomic encoder-decoder using a variational autoencoder (VAE)\"; \"widely used pathology foundation models\""}]}
